 "evidence": "A",
 "licence_note": null,
 "history": "The 1751 Clothing Warrant fixed the cut of the British private's coat: red, lapels of the regiment's facing colour to the waist, small round cuffs, the skirts hooked back, the buttonholes bound with the regiment's worsted lace (Morier's grenadier paintings of 1751) [S17][S4]. A detachment of the 22nd Foot, red faced buff, wintered at the German Flatts in 1758 (Capt. Philip Townsend's letter of 1 March) [S16]. Its lace pattern is not confirmed, so the loops are plain white tape. Howe's cut-down coats came only in the summer of 1758.",
